  For an early wizard throwing Expert daggers they're game breakers.
Str:25 gives +6 damage bonus, and range 10 for thrown missiles.
Expert daggers average 2x per fling.  That's an average of +12 damage
just from the strength bonus, and at range, wield what you like and
wear the best enchanted shield you can find.

  GoP do restrict spell casting some, but an early wizard has a lot of
trouble surviving on offensive spell casting in combat.  When not in
combat the GoP can easily be removed (takes one turn) for offline
spell casting, then reworn (another turn).  Players don't really spend
that much time in combat.

  Using the GoP for massive thrown dagger damage saves Pw that would
otherwise be used in combat.  Pw that can be used for offline spells:
light, haste self, identify, knock, lock, protection, charm monster,
etc.  There's only one school of attack spells, and many schools of
non-attack spells.


